defs: SRC := $HERMES_CONTEXT_SRC, default /opt/data/workspace/hermes-context/; DST := $HERMES_CONTEXT_DST, default /workspace/hermes-context/; A9_mirror := ∀ path ∈ SRC -> identical path in DST, recursive, matching file contents ∧ directory structure ∧ symlinks (metadata/timestamps/hardlinks out-of-scope)
invariants:
  A2_oneway: sync = host(SRC) -> workspace(DST), one-way; ∀ mode -> nothing writes to SRC
  A4_fallback: ∀ run -> if rsync ∉ PATH then cp -a/tar-pipe fallback, equal A9 semantics; sync CONTENTS of SRC into DST (src/ -> dst), no nesting
  A5_mirror: ∀ mode -> DST end state == SRC end state, stale entries DELETED (rsync --delete; cp path reconciles identically)
  A6_dryrun: --dry-run -> ZERO writes ∀ targets incl. logs; DST byte-identical pre/post
  A7_recursive: A5 recursive ∀ depth; stale subtrees deleted ∀ depth; README states this correctly
  A8_placement: log ∈ ~/.cache/hermes-context (or $HERMES_CONTEXT_LOG) always OUTSIDE DST, no exceptions; install paths (∼/.local/bin | /workspace/hdcs/bin) OUTSIDE mirrored tree; sync never deletes own entrypoints
  A9_class: verify contents+structure+symlinks recursively; mismatch -> exit nonzero (never warn+exit0); metadata complaints out-of-scope
  A11_guard: reject/clean-no-op when SRC==DST; ∀ destructive op on DST -> verified staging copy of SRC exists first; stage -> verify -> touch DST (order = law)
  A12_identity: guard via realpath not strings; refuse (nonzero, no writes) when realpath(SRC)==realpath(DST) ∨ ancestor/descendant ∨ DST resolves through symlink into SRC; both paths, pre-destructive
  A13_verified: verified := content-compared (A9 class) vs SRC; non-emptiness ≠ verification; staging verification fail -> nonzero exit
  A10_bar: FAIL only on defects reachable in normal op (default config, documented usage, plausible misconfig losing/corrupting data); exotic triggers -> KNOWN_LIMITATIONS with repro notes
deliverable_set := {sync-hermes-context.sh, hermes-context.service, hermes-context.timer, README.md} in one artifact dir
units := systemd USER units (systemctl --user), timer 6h, no root; script standalone-capable (cron/installer callable)
open:
  KNOWN_LIMITATIONS: exotic corpora (newline-in-filename); hostile env combos (DST->log dir) — repro notes in packet, non-blocking per A10
  +validation: verify A9 class ∩ A6 (dry-run byte-identity) ∩ A12 guards ∩ A13 staging gate via test matrix
